<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Monroe returns six weeks after the three-month visit, having had six sessions of pelvic floor physical therapy. She does her home program most days. Pain with intercourse is now mild and occasional, and her worst pelvic pain in the past week was 2 of 10. She continues the continuous pill with no periods and has used naproxen on two days this month. Her repeat transvaginal ultrasound this morning was reviewed by Dr. Okoye. She has had no thoughts of suicide or self-harm. She and her spouse want to begin trying for a pregnancy in about eight months, and she asks what the steps will be. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Physical therapy</td><td>Six sessions; home program most days</td></tr><tr><td>Pain</td><td>Worst 2 of 10; mild, occasional pain with intercourse</td></tr><tr><td>Treatment</td><td>Continuous combined pill; naproxen on two days this month</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>PHQ-9 4, GAD-7 3</td></tr><tr><td>Pregnancy plans</td><td>Would like to begin trying in about eight months</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

