<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Endometriosis with a left ovarian endometrioma (N80.102)</content>. Well controlled. The repeat ultrasound shows the left endometrioma at 3.1 by 2.6 cm, slightly smaller, with the same typical features and no deep disease. Dr. Okoye reviewed it and agrees that no surgery is needed. Pregnancy plan: a preconception visit before she stops the pill in about eight months; folic acid continues; endometriosis pain may return off the pill, and naproxen should be stopped once she could be pregnant; reproductive endocrinology referral if she is not pregnant after six months of trying, or sooner if pain returns strongly. [S]<list><item>Continue the continuous combined pill until the preconception visit.</item><item>Ultrasound yearly, or sooner if pain changes.</item><item>Preconception visit in about seven months.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Pelvic floor muscle dysfunction with myofascial pain (M62.89)</content>. Much improved after six sessions. [S]<list><item>Two more sessions, then the home program.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Major depressive disorder, single episode, moderate (F32.1)</content>. PHQ-9 4: remission, with cognitive behavioral therapy. GAD-7 3. Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide or self-harm; the safety plan stays in her phone. [S]<list><item>Therapy monthly for several months to prevent relapse.</item><item>PHQ-9 at each visit.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Pelvic pain score (0 to 10), pain with intercourse and bowel movements, and missed working days</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Worst pain 2 of 10; mild, occasional pain with intercourse; no missed work</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Bleeding pattern on continuous suppression</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No periods</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Combined pill: adherence, side effects, and reasons to stop estrogen (migraine with aura, high blood pressure, clot symptoms, smoking)</td><td>Every visit, with blood pressure</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Taken daily; blood pressure 112/70; no migraine with aura or clot symptoms</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Naproxen: days used each month, and stomach or kidney symptoms</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Two days this month</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>No opioid, benzodiazepine, or sleep-medicine accumulation; prescription monitoring program</td><td>At the start, then every visit while pain is active</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No opioid, benzodiazepine or sleep medicine</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Transvaginal ultrasound: endometrioma size and deep disease</td><td>At diagnosis; repeat at about four months on medical treatment, then yearly or if symptoms change</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Left endometrioma 3.1 by 2.6 cm, slightly smaller; no deep disease; next yearly</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Pelvic examination</td><td>At diagnosis, and when pain persists or changes</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Pelvic floor relaxed; slight left tenderness</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Surgical evaluation (laparoscopic excision)</td><td>If pain does not respond to medical treatment, the cyst grows, or imaging is atypical</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Pain controlled and the cyst slightly smaller</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Pelvic floor physical therapy</td><td>Weekly for six to eight weeks</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Six sessions; two more, then the home program</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Pregnancy intention and fertility plan</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Wants to begin trying in about eight months; preconception visit planned; reproductive endocrinology after six months of trying</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression measure (PHQ-9)</td><td>Monthly during acute treatment, every 2 to 4 weeks in continuation, then periodically</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 4: remission</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Anxiety measure (GAD-7)</td><td>At diagnosis and with each depression measure</td><td>Completed today</td><td>GAD-7 3</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Suicide-risk review, safety plan, lethal means, and the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No thoughts of suicide or self-harm; safety plan current</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Cognitive behavioral therapy engagement</td><td>Monthly in continuation</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Moving to monthly sessions</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Sleep without sedatives</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Seven to eight hours without a sleep aid</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Worst pelvic pain 3 of 10 or less, and no missed working days for pain, by four months. Outcome by 1956-10-26: Worst pain 2 of 10; no missed working days for two months [S]</item><item>No opioid, benzodiazepine or sleep-medicine prescription, and naproxen on 10 days a month or fewer. Outcome by 1956-10-26: None prescribed; naproxen on two or three days a month; diphenhydramine stopped [S]</item><item>PHQ-9 score below 5 by four months. Outcome by 1956-10-26: PHQ-9 4 [S]</item><item>A written plan for when and how to try for a pregnancy, made with her before the four-month visit. Outcome by 1956-10-26: Plan made: stop the pill when ready to try, after a preconception visit; reproductive endocrinology referral if not pregnant within six months [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Practice Bulletin No. 114: Management of Endometriosis (2010); ESHRE guideline: endometriosis (2022); Chronic Pelvic Pain: ACOG Practice Bulletin, Number 218 (2020); CDC Clinical Practice Guideline for Prescribing Opioids for Pain, United States, 2022 (2022); U.S. Medical Eligibility Criteria for Contraceptive Use, 2024 (2024); Anxiety Disorders in Adults: Screening (2023); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Two more physical therapy sessions. Behavioral health monthly. Preconception visit in about seven months; endometriosis review sooner if pain returns. [S]</paragraph></text>

